WEBVTT

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:03.410
Yo!

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.730
I got tired of waiting for you, Tomoya-kun.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.490
So much so that it almost felt like a week.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.690
Iori?

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:13.740
Hashima...

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.290
Why are you here?

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:20.010
Because we agreed to meet here, of course.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.690
We agreed with Izumi-chan!

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.630
You weren't invited!

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.500
There's no need to panic.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.820
Izumi is here.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.540
As my circle's...

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.430
...secret weapon!

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.750
<i>Azuki bean soup?</i>

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.300
Izumi-chan...?

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.350
Hashima... Izumi...

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.030
Izumi-cha-

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.750
Tomoya-senpai.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.420
I...

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.280
I...

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.620
Thank you for your message, Izumi-chan.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:01.810
We haven't seen since the pool, have we?

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:02.680
No!

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.090
You helped me out so much on that occasion, Megumi-senpai!

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:11.210
It was very kind of you to come here today in spite of the sudden invitation.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.500
I'm cold now!

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.140
Sweet...

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.150
So, what in the world is this about?

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:02.530
It appears that you played the demo version of our, rouge en rouge's, new winter Comiket game?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.560
I'm open for any impressions and suggestions you have.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.440
By the way, the "like" button is he-

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.040
Stop messing around!

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:15.000
This is simply a rip-off of the basic idea for our, Blessing Software's, new game!

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.380
I already told you last summer, didn't I?

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.330
That the game is on.

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.650
Are you planning to destroy us?

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.440
If a big circle like rouge en rouge puts out a game in the same genre,

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.100
a small player like us will be eaten alive.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.430
I wonder.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.360
If several circles release works in the same genre,

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.530
we can make people think that the genre itself has momentum.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:37.500
I think that there's a way for both of us to win.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.730
If that actually was your intention.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:46.240
Well, even if I were to agree for now...

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.320
At least stop dragging Izumi-chan into it!

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.370
Your unsightly ambition is not something the pure-

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:54.380
...growing-

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.280
...extremely talented Izumi-chan should be involved in!

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.880
Thank you, Tomoya-senpai,

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:06.180
for saying that someone as inexperienced as me is growing and talented and cute.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.060
He didn't say that last one.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.060
He definitely didn't.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.600
But I'm sorry.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.870
This is something I asked of Onii-chan.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:17.680
That I wanted to fight on the same terms as your circle, Senpai.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.370
I've had a hard time thanks to you!

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.690
I've been looking for a writer who can make a romance game.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:26.950
In the end, I lured the whole scenario team from a famous game circle to join us instead.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.000
Why?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.790
Why do you do this, Izumi-chan?

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.470
Because...

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:36.380
Didn't you make doujin because you wanted to honour the works you love?

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.000
Didn't you start making doujin not because of popularity or money,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:44.720
but because you just wanted to deepen your camaraderie with those who love the same works as you do?

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:50.100
I remember the times when you read manga and laughed with me-

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.390
When you played games and cried-

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:55.350
When you sold doujinshi and cried-

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.360
And what are you doi-

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:01.480
I'm sorry, Tomoya-senpai.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:06.860
But...

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:11.120
I can't fight with Sawamura-senpai otherwise.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.040
Eriri?

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:20.500
I see, so you became the main artist of rouge en rouge.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:21.460
Congratulations.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:25.150
You've advanced a lot in just a few months.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:29.280
I ask you to fight me seriously with no holding back at winter Comiket,

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.970
Kashiwagi Eri-sensei.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:34.030
It's not like I can hold back.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:35.780
Thank you very much.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:40.730
You see, I'm against a big shot famous circle, rouge en rouge.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.100
If I don't show a considerable difference in ability,

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.990
I'll end up losing just due to the different standings of our circles.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.990
The level of the circle has nothing to do with it!

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.760
Hey, Iori.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.010
What did you tell Izumi-chan about Eriri?

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:56.330
No, nothing about that.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.370
Stop lying!

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:02.090
There's no way the kind Izumi-chan would show her hostility towards Eriri so openly otherwise.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:05.200
Well, I suppose she's just getting what she asked for.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.650
No way!

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:09.840
Though certainly, Eriri is bad-tempered, turns on you easily,

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.870
holds a grudge forever, and is flawed as both a doujin author and a human being!

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:16.100
That sounds really flawed.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.290
Well, I'm looking forward to it.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.930
Just be careful that you won't be crushed under your circle's signboard.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:24.940
And you, too.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.760
Don't get passed by a no-name shooting-star author before you even know it,

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:34.260
degenerating into an "illustrator" who just hangs on Twitter all day long without actually drawing anything.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.320
You small fry!

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:38.410
Same to you!

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:38.930
Hey!

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:39.760
Damn you!

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:40.470
What?!

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:42.250
Damn you!

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.880
Should we stop them soon?

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.760
Right, on my count.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:52.060
Ow...

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.000
Hang in there.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.200
And so,

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.350
let's both do our best for winter Comiket, Tomoya-kun.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.130
No matter what you'll do,

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:03.140
we, Blessing Software, will not lose, Iori.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:05.240
You sure are full of confidence.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:07.530
A game combines all art forms.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:10.130
There's more to our match than the illustrations.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:11.860
Well, that's certainly true.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:15.870
And we have yet another ultimate secret weapon.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.190
I see.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:18.290
Kasumi Utako, huh?

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.120
Yes!

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.190
So the scenario of our game will definitely be-

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:23.320
I wonder.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:24.500
What?

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:29.010
Rather, if anything, the scenario is something I'm quite certain we won't lose in.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.510
What?

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:32.590
Let's go home, Izumi.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:33.330
Ah.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:34.440
Yes!

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.140
Well then, Megumi-senpai!

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:37.460
See you, Izumi-chan!

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:38.640
Wait a moment, Iori!

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.640
It's Kasumi Utako.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:45.150
The author of Metronome of Love.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.400
Tomoya-kun, you said it yourself.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.570
A game combines all art forms.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.000
Here, curry bread and coffee.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:12.900
Thanks.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.890
What's with that married couple?

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.970
So, having read it again,

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:25.150
did you find out anything new about Kasumigaoka-senpai's scenario?

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.180
She really is a god.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:33.010
Should I say "sure thing, fanboy" in this situation?

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:34.680
Sure, if you want to troll me,

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.910
but being trolled like that IRL is pretty irritating.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.600
Are you maybe, thinking about it too much?

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.410
It looks very good to me, too.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:44.010
But...

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:46.130
Iori said it to me back then.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:51.130
<i>Rather, if anything, the scenario is something I'm quite certain we won't lose in.</i>

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.240
He is just a doujin thug.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:57.140
He's a piece of trash who doesn't care about how good or interesting something is,

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:01.550
but only judges its merits by whether it will sell or not.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:05.270
But precisely because of that, if he says that they can win,

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:08.430
their work is bound to win commercially.

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:09.650
Katou, I-

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:11.970
Huh?

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:15.120
Hey, Yoshihiko, where did Katou go?

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:19.640
She took her stuff and said she's moving back to her parents'.

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:25.370
So, what did you want to ask me instead of Aki-kun?

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.600
W-Well, um...

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.880
How is Morals-kun doing?

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:34.980
Um, you want to ask me instead of Aki-kun?

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:35.860
That's right.

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:36.880
Is that bad?

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.810
Well, I guess it's fine.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:44.270
Well, he's been reading your scenario all the time.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.890
He still hasn't finished?

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:49.680
No, he's read it countless times, and seems to be troubled.

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:51.070
T-Troubled?

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:57.660
When you made him decide,
it put him under a lot of pressure.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.660
S-So, has he decided?

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:03.790
It seems he's reading it over
and over again because he can't.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.330
I-I see.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:08.360
M-Maybe that means that he still wishes for something...

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:10.000
What is going on?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.880
W-What do you mean?

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.400
All your reactions have been cute,

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:16.590
and not at all like you.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:19.220
While you are not wrong about that,

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:23.430
being told that so bluntly is quite irritating.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.560
Well, be that as it may,

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:28.270
what do you mean by "still wishes for something"?

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.270
It's no use telling you.

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:37.280
Or rather, if I told you, it'd end up being meaningless.

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:52.540
U-Um, Katou?

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:54.820
Katou-san?

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.850
Hm, what?

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:59.050
Why are you suddenly so into it?

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:02.430
That's not like your usual flat, haphazard self.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:05.330
Not only is your observation wrong,

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:09.180
but being told that in such an insensitive manner pisses me off.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:13.470
If that's what you think, you should get angry more seriously.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:15.430
Hey, Aki-kun.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:16.370
What is it?

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:22.700
I wonder what meaning Kasumigaoka-senpai wrote into these two scenarios.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:24.190
Meaning?

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:28.370
What happens when you pick one of them?

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:29.380
I don't know.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:35.100
<i>And what should I do in the future?</i>

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:39.170
And anyway, if I'm told to pick the one I like...

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:43.700
There's no scenario by Utaha-senpai I wouldn't like.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.770
Sure thing, fanboy.

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:52.230
In the end, I might not know without playing them.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:54.440
That's it, Aki-kun!

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:56.690
What is, Katou-kun?

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.920
If you don't know without playing,

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:00.580
then you just have to play it!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:01.820
It's the weekend, too!

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:05.240
But this scenario hasn't yet been included in the game at all...

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:07.320
So let's include it.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:08.410
Katou...

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.320
Take this.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:18.310
I'll pick up a change of clothes
and come to your place in an hour.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:21.730
Let's make it playable before this week is up.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:25.170
Katou!

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:32.770
You know, I should be the one saying that.

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:39.780
Aki-kun?

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.130
Hm?

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:43.710
How far in are you now?

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:45.280
Well...

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.740
Perhaps 20 percent of the whole thing.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:50.280
That's all we got done in one night?

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:55.460
Maybe finishing it in just two days really was too much to ask for.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:56.790
Maybe.

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:59.380
Was this all for nothing?

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:01.670
Was it all pointless?

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.780
How about resting for a while?

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:05.300
Sorry, Aki-kun.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.630
I got so excited for nothing yesterday,

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:10.220
and now I'm being a downer for nothing.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:12.100
It is useful.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.350
It's not pointless.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.060
Huh?

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:15.820
It's okay.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:18.450
You weren't wrong about anything.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.820
Why do you think so?

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:25.970
You don't know whether a scenario for a game is good or bad without playing it as a game.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:28.820
Intertwining pictures illustrating the scenario, music bringing it to life,

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:32.080
and the scripting which makes it all work...

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:35.700
All of them support each other, and make the story into something more.

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.960
That's what a visual novel is all about.

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:43.080
We are definitely headed in the right direction!

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:45.840
So Katou, don't worry.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:03.660
So it's like this?

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:05.490
So it was like this?!

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:09.340
Being a 2D otaku was just a cover?!

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:13.070
You lying normie!

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.610
Huh, Hyoudou-san?

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:18.340
What, Katou-chan?

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:19.120
What's this about?

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.240
Since when have you two been like this?

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:25.260
Um, since last night, I suppose.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.380
We came here straight from school.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.890
So it's your first morning together?

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:34.710
It's day already, though.

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:39.070
Katou, only exchange information after waking up properly first.

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.650
I see, you've gathered here to work on the game.

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:46.240
So, does it look like you'll make it?

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.940
Not doing that well.

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:50.290
I see.

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:52.320
That's bad!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.570
Ah, give me a break, what a shock!

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:58.880
But you really are a great deal of help, Michiru.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:14:59.830
I know, right?

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:03.590
If I hadn't come, you two would just have happily slept on.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:07.510
No, I wasn't talking about your help in the past,

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:09.620
but in the future!

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:13.010
Wait a minute.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.510
What are you talking about, Tomo?

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.520
That's right,

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:18.490
since we have you, we can turn this desperate situation around,

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:20.580
and go for a great comeback!

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:23.520
What? I can only play the guitar!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.030
I can't help with smashing the keyboard!

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:28.870
Don't worry, Michiru.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:32.780
You have an essential role which only you can fulfil!

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.740
Good morning, ladies of Icy Tail.

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:45.880
Your duties today will be related to helping us, Blessing Software, create our new game!

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:46.360
Hey!

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:47.130
Hey, hey!

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.880
Wait, Akki!

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:49.810
Toki.

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:52.720
Please leave any questions until after I'm finished.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:57.450
We rushed here because you said we had to talk about an important life-or-death issue for the band.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.980
So why are we making a game now?

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.690
What is this about, Micchi?

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:08.430
Well, Tomo asked me to have you come over for whatever reason I could come up with.

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:10.320
You tricked us, Micchi!

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:14.820
No, this really is an important
life-or-death issue for the band.

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:17.920
Because unless you help us,

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:20.660
I will step down as the manager of the band.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:23.250
I won't arrange any concerts or escort you there!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.080
What? That's mean!

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.840
So let's do our best for the existence of Icy Tail!

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:31.340
Why us?

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.890
That's a good question!

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:39.100
Because you Icy Tail possess a unique weapon other bands don't!

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.600
Not only are all of you otaku,

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:45.100
but you're also proficient with computers!

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:47.110
Apart from Michiru.

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:47.800
What?

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:50.290
What does that have to do with the band?

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:53.860
In short, you want us to do odd jobs on a computer?

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:54.900
Yeah.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:56.690
You've all been tempered in your band,

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:59.290
so I'm sure one all-nighter will be no big deal for you.

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:03.000
So you're planning to work us hard the whole weekend?

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.360
Do your best, everybody!

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:07.290
That's not good!

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.780
Sleeping over at a guy's place...

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:11.020
It's okay!

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.010
This is indeed my home,

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.010
but Michiru practically lives here too!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.700
Also, many girls have slept over here before,

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.680
and no mistakes have happened.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.810
If that's the case, that's rather a problem for you as a man.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:24.510
Please, guys!

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:27.130
This is a really serious affair for our circle!

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.830
B-But I have something important to do tomorrow.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:33.690
Echika.

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:37.120
Is it more important than helping your friend who's in trouble?

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:38.450
It totally is!

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.820
I haven't gone on a date in a long time-

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:48.260
All right, let's get to work, then.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:49.820
Do you have computers for us?

00:17:49.820 --> 00:17:53.170
Ah, Katou is on her way to Eriri's house to borrow some.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:54.920
Hey, wait a moment.

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:57.140
Do you guys really want to do it?

00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:58.290
Please, Echika.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.350
Help us, Echika.

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:00.930
Let's do it, Echika.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:05.230
Even if you members were to fight or break up with your boyfriends,

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.980
it's of no concern to our office.

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:09.810
You guys!

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:12.690
I'm borrowing these, then.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:16.030
Sorry that I can't help, Megumi.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.020
Not at all.

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:20.200
Lending laptops is a great deal of help already.

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.770
And you have to work hard on the art, too.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:26.290
You're right.

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:27.740
Doing well?

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:29.060
Kind of.

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:30.260
I see.

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:32.200
So let's both do our best.

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:32.770
Yeah!

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:34.050
Leave it to me!

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:53.930
Leave it to me, huh?

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:15.650
What is this?

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:20.400
I see...

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:24.440
So that's what it was?

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.710
Hello everyone!

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:07.200
We're Icy Tail!

00:22:11.190 --> 00:22:13.670
Did you finally read it?

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:17.750
That is my duty as the director, after all.

00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:19.490
I see.

00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:25.740
So, Morals-kun,

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:27.510
which one did you choose?

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:29.230
The first version?

00:22:29.230 --> 00:22:30.990
Or the second version?

00:22:32.230 --> 00:22:33.220
Meguri?

00:22:33.770 --> 00:22:36.680
Or... Ruri?

00:22:41.510 --> 00:22:43.250
I'm not choosing either.

00:22:43.890 --> 00:22:45.260
It needs another take.

00:22:46.650 --> 00:22:49.160
This is a shitty game.
